Crazy idea, but were you wielding a pickaxe or mattock? What seems to
have happened there was that your characer started doing a multi-turn
action for no apparent reason, and without a message. My first thought
after reading the thread was that it was an autodig accident, but
source-surfing apparently reveals that that would have caused
messages. I've been systematically running through the source to see
things that could potentially make you miss turns without messages;
there aren't many. Being hit by Magicbane and scared as a result
causes you to miss two turns with no additional message (which could
explain the results shown), except that every monster that hits you in
that log has its weapon accounted for. Multiple-turn engraving gives
no messages that single-turn doesn't, but the log doesn't show you
doing that either. One weirder possibility is that you hit the 2-turn
paralysis from vomiting as a result, perhaps, of eating a rotten egg
several turns earlier; that gives no messages, but paralyzes you
anyway, if you happen to be sickness-resistant at the time (this is
arguably a bug). I can't find any other cases where the introduction
of paralysis can happen without a message.

The other possibility is that of a typo; I can sort-of envisage that
sort of result due to hitting a count before entering a command (if
you were spacing through messages, a different typo wouldn't have
caused the problem). Or perhaps you had rest_on_space on (probably by
accident; doing it is deliberately is a bad idea for precisely this
reason) and hit space too many times spacing through the messages,
which would have produced the log shown and where you might not have
noticed anything was wrong.

